	(text "OOMWOO cliff sensor board (rev 1, 2026-10-28). One design, fitted 6x. No lenses: narrow-beam 5 mm parts (IR333-A 20 deg,\nPT333-3B black lens) tilted toward each other so their beams cross at the floor. The tilt sets the reference distance:\ncrossing depth = (spacing / 2) / tan(tilt), e.g. 18 mm spacing: 30 deg -> 15.6 mm, 25 deg -> 19.3 mm, 20 deg -> 24.7 mm.\nBeyond the crossing point the beams diverge, so a far floor (a cliff) returns little light even if it is white.\nThe main board switches the LED cathode (CLIFF_LED_EN, modulate it to cancel ambient light) and pulls OUT up (47k).\nRefs 85xx: unique on the OOMWOO panel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8c216909-1227-479f-aa0d-50967425e521")
	)
	(text "Assembly (JLC): D8501 and Q8501 THT with the assembly standoff (~2 mm) so the leads can be bent;\npin bending to the tilt angle, or bend by hand in the 3D-printed housing. LED: flat side = cathode.\nQ8501: flat side / square pad = emitter. Spacing D8501-Q8501: 18 mm centre to centre."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f2cc1633-cc06-42c7-affb-e20f6b0a3aba")
	)
